n  Called to OR by Dr  Yeh   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received in formalin in a single container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   patient s name and medical record number  It consists of a double wire  localized excisional breast biopsy which has been six inked by the surgeon   The specimen measures 11 0cm from lateral to medial  6 1cm from anterior to  posterior  and 2 9cm from superior to inferior  Two wires are present within  the specimen  Wire  1 enters the specimen at the anteroinferior margin  1 4cm  from the medial margin  0 9cm from the superior margin  and 2 3cm from the  lateral margin  Wire  2 courses superficially along the anterior aspect of the  specimen from lateral to medial  approximately equidistant from the superior  and inferior margins  This wire is dislodged during processing of the  specimen  Three sutures are present in the specimen  a short suture marks the  superior aspect of the specimen  a long suture marks the lateral aspect  and a  whip stitch marks the posterior aspect  per surgeon  the chest wall margin    The specimen has been radiographed by the surgeon and orientation of the  specimen is correlated with the radiograph  Based on this correlation  the  clip is located nearest to the medial margin and the calcifications present in  the radiograph are located posteromedially  The specimen is serially sectioned  from medial to lateral into 10 slices  slice  1 represents the medial margin    slice  10 the lateral margin   In slice  2  there is a red brown hemorrhagic  area clip which may represent the core biopsy site  This is located 1 1cm  from the superior  0 8cm from the medial  2 9cm from the posterior  2 2cm  from the anterior  10 2cm from the lateral  and 0 7cm from the inferior  margin  A firm  tan nodule is present in slices  3 and  4  located at the  medial margin  1 4cm from the superior margin  1 8cm from the inferior  margin  3 8cm from the posterior margin  7 0cm from the lateral margin  and  2 0cm from the anteri