Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 48 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  95   EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  5   EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  NOTE  Vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 55                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm yellow fibrofatty tissue fragment with localizing wire in place and an accompanying x ray  inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 4cm in greatest dimension stellate  irregular firm tan lesion  grossly extending to within 0 4cm of an inked margin  The suspicious area is submitted entirely in cassettes A through C  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassettes D through G  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  SUSPICIOUS LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Horace C  Wu  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY IES   Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  CARRASCO  RUBEN  D   M D  PH D   DIAGNOSIS  by CARRASCO RUBEN D  M D  PH D   LEFT BREAST  CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY   ATYPICAL LYMPHOID INFILTRATE  See note   The specimen consists of breast tissue containing predominantly stroma  and scant amount of ductal epithelium  The stroma is very focally involved  by an atypical lymphoid infiltrate consisting of large cells present in  small cluster  The large atypical cell are characterized by a vesicular  nuclei  prominent  1 to 3 nucleoli and moderate amount of cytoplasm  Rare  apoptotic bodies and mitotic figures are noted among the large atypical  cells   Small lymphocytes are also present and occur primarily around breast  epithelial structures   Immunoperoxidase studies performed on paraffin tissue sections reveal the  large cells to be reactive for LCA   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the B cell markers  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a and weakely positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   very faint staining   Substantial  tissue was lost from the slide stained for bcl 6  but nuclear positivity  was seen in the large cells  Staining for immunoglobulin kappa   lambda  light chains is difficult to interprete due to high background but appear  to show an excess of lambda membrane staining of the large cells  The  small lymphocytes are positive for LCA   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the T cell marker  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Staining for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  highlights endothelial cells and some fibrous stromal  cells  Staining for Cytokeratin  panK highlights breast epithelium   NOTE  The infiltrate is atypical and composed of large cells reactive  for LCA   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the B cell markers  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a  The findings are  highly suspicious for involvement of the breast tissue by large B cell  lymphoma  however  given the limited nature of this specimen  the sparse  atypical infiltrate present  and an equivocal staining for immunoglobuling  light chains  a definitive diagnosis is not possible  Suggest correlation  with additional clinical information and laboratory studies including  additional tissue sampling of another involved site if clinically  indicated   CLINICAL DATA   History  FNA of left breast at MGH showed atypical lymphoid proliferation   favor large cell type   Operation  11 G Ultrasound guided  Operative findings  Vague hypoechoic mass  Clinical Diagnosis  Lyphoma  Breast image findings  ill defined   TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  Left breast tissue in a yellow cassette  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by LAZAR ALEXANDER J M D  PH D   The specimen is received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit  number  and  Lt  breast   in a single yellow cassette  and consists of  multiple  soft  fragmented  yellow to white tissue cores  1 4 x REMOVED_DATE 2cm in  aggregate    Micro 1  Yellow cassette labeled  Lt  breast   Multi frags  ESS   Reports to  GADD  MICHELE  A M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY IES    report_end  , No.
