 REMOVED_CASE_ID  RICHARD KATHLEEN M 50 F  REG REF 01 07    REMOVED_CASE_ID   WIC GOODMAN LOIS S  M D                                                                                             Specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  SOUT Received  01 07 10  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Spec Type    Clinical diagnosis   history  Left lower breast nodule Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  guided breast biopsy  left breast  designated  left breast lower nodule  and consists of three firm  tan white  glistening needle biopsies ranging in size from 1 2cm  in length x 0 2cm  in diameter to 1 5cm  in length x 0 2cm  in diameter  The specimens are marked with blue ink  3X all  Total fixation time is 14 hours  Dictated by  LV Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD DIAGNOSIS  Left breast  lower  biopsy  Sclerotic fibroadenoma with a focus of florid usual ductal hyperplasia  See note  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUK REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUK REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUK DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT  NOTE  The core biopsy consists predominantly of a sclerotic fibroadenoma  At one edge of the fibroadenoma is a small focus of florid usual ductal hyperplasia  The hyperplastic cells have streaming nuclei and show maturation  features of UDH   Immunohistochemical stains of the area show cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE with rare weakly positive cells and estrogen receptor with strong positivity at the periphery of the duct but less intense staining in the center of the duct  Although the IHC pattern is inconclusive  the histomorphology is most consistent with usual ductal hyperplasia  Final Diagnosis by  Kenan J  Sauder  M D  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUK REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUK Notes  REMOVED_DATE  KS showed this case to all pathologists both before IHC results and after  DF and RS did not see IHC results  and all agree that UDH  not ADH  is present  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUKCODES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Left breast  NO Sclerosis  NOS  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Left breast  NO Fibroadenoma  N BREANBX    BREANBX BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Intraductal hyp Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUK REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUK REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUK REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUKCOPIES TO  CAHILL TERESA M D  NWH RADIOLOGY DEPT  NEWTON  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   617 243  REMOVED_CASE_ID  GOODMAN LOIS S  M D  GYNECOLOGY PARTNERS WESTON  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   781 899  REMOVED_CASE_ID MARKERS  Breast Disease Related Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORDPROCEDURES  IMMUNOCYTO  01 11 10  REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUK   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   01 08 10  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUK REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD SAUKTISSUES  Breast  needle biopsy   left lower Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORDFinal  ABBOTT TODD MD   REMOVED_DATE  01 11 10  REMOVED_CASE_ID   by MD ABBT SAUDER KENAN J  MD   REMOVED_DATE  01 11 10  REMOVED_CASE_ID   by MD SAUK                                                                                              , No.
