tors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm left breast biopsy containing a 1 5cm tan firm lesion  1 0cm from the inked margin  A portion is given to Dr  Sgroi for research  A representative mass and closest margin  submitted in A through C  with surrounding representative sections in D through G  Labeled  A  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm linear piece of fibrofatty tissue  entirely submitted in cassette H  Labeled  Left axillary contents  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary node dissection containing multiple pink to tan lymph nodes  The largest measuring 0 8cm in greatest dimension  Submitted entirely in cassettes I through K  Labeled  Additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue containing REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan to pink lymph node  entirely submitted in cassette L  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAG