al to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm circumscribed hemorrhagic cavity that has a heterogenous bloody and white cut surface in the central portion of the breast  The cavity measures 3 5cm to the closest posterior margin and 3cm to the closest anterior margin  Located 3 5cm superior medial to this cavity located in the upper inner quadrant  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm stellate firm lesion that is 3 2cm to the closest posterior and 3 1cm to the closest anterior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is fibrous with areas of gray granular fibrous tissue and bright yellow discoloration located primarily in the upper inner and lower inner quadrants  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative radial section of closest posterior margin to the hemorrhage cavity in the central breast cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire cavity in the central breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections to closest posterior margin for mass in upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of mass in upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of firm area in upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire firm bright yellow lesion in left inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of gray granular fibrous tissue from left inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire nipple  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 24   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 12 29PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  Addendum  1  Additional immunohistochemistry A repeated immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   demonstrates positive staining for ductal cells in areas of DCIS and negative staining in areas of invasive l